      "message": "## Benefits of this interface\n\nThanks to this interface, we can simplify some of the processing originally written in this change: [125509 - PostAlgoPathValidator](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/125509/4/pce/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/pce/graph/PostAlgoPathValidator.java#1083)\n\nBy altering the signature of `computeAssignableSpectrum` to return an instance of  `AssignableSpectrum`, we can get rid of the need to manipulate the parameter `centerFreqGranularityCollection` in the method `computeSpectrumOccupation`.\n\nAlso, `getSpectrumAssignment()` doesn\u0027t need this code which means we can also get rid of the extra `isFlexGrid \u003d true`:\n\n````\nboolean isFlexGrid \u003d true;\nCollection centerFrequencyGranularityCollection \u003d \n    new CenterFrequencyGranularityCollection(50);\nBitSet assignableBitset \u003d computeSpectrumOccupation(path, allPceNodes,\n    spectralWidthSlotNumber, subscriber, centerFrequencyGranularityCollection);\n```\n\n## Interface implementations\n\nNote that there are two implementations of this interface:\n1. [DefaultAssignableSpectrum](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/126575/3/pce/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/pce/graph/DefaultAssignableSpectrum.java)\n2. [EmptyAssignableSpectrum](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/126575/3/pce/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/pce/graph/EmptyAssignableSpectrum.java#20)\n\n### In short\n\n- An instance of.`DefaultAssignableSpectrum` is returned in normal operation, when a frequency range is found.\n- `EmptyAssignableSpectrum` is returned in all other cases.",
