      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T19:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "## Overview\nThe refactor in this relation chain centers around `AssignableSpectrum computeAssignableSpectrum() {...}` on line 1080 in this class. The refactor is an alternate solution to [125509 - Adjust PostAlgoValidator.getSpectrumAssignement](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/125509)\n\n1. Before this refactor, `computeAssignableSpectrum` was called `getSpectrumAssignment`.\n2. `getSpectrumAssignment` returned an instance of `SpectrumAssignment`\n3. It is my understanding, that change [Adjust PostAlgoValidator.getSpectrumAssignement](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/125509) aimed at adding a separate method returning a `BitSet`, while getSpectrumAssignment still returns a SpectrumAssignment.\n\nAlso, in [125823](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/125823/2/pce/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/pce/graph/PostAlgoPathValidator.java#142) the path is processed twice with the same inputs. The solution below mitigates that.\n\n## Suggested alternate solution\n\nInstead, I propose returning an object that can serve *both* a `SpectrumAssignment` object and a `BitSet`. \n\nThe object `assignableSpectrum` is an instance of [AssignableSpectrum](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/126575/3/pce/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/pce/graph/AssignableSpectrum.java) (used on line 119) and therefore has two methods; one returning `SpectrumAssignment` and one returning `BitSet`:\n\n1. `computeBestSpectrumAssignment()`, returning `SpectrumAssignment` (called on line 124). This gives the same result as the old `getSpectrumAssignment()`\n2. `availableBitSet()`, returning `BitSet`, suitable as a solution in the change \"Pce orchestration Step 1\" in change [125823](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/125823)\n\nSo in `PostAlgoPathValidator` in change [125823](https://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/transportpce/+/125823/2/pce/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/transportpce/pce/graph/PostAlgoPathValidator.java#142), instead of...\n\n```\nspectrumOccupation \u003d computeSpectrumOccupation(path, allPceNodes, \n    spectralWidthSlotNumber, subscriber, \n    new CenterFrequencyGranularityCollection(50));\n```\n\n... you can use ...\n\n```\nspectrumOccupation \u003d assignableSpectrum.availableBitSet();\n```\n\nThe full example is then:\n\n```\nAssignableSpectrum assignableSpectrum \u003d computeAssignableSpectrum(\n    path,\n    allPceNodes,\n    spectralWidthSlotNumber,\n    subscriber);\nspectrumAssignment \u003d assignableSpectrum.computeBestSpectrumAssignment(subscriber);\nspectrumOccupation \u003d assignableSpectrum.availableBitSet();\n```",
